di-framework embedded PGlite component

The provider bundles PostgreSQL 17.11 built for WASI. The engine source is
upstream PostgreSQL REL_17_11 (commit 083ac033419f690758508e08c1736089384bbee8)
with ElectricSQL's PGlite WASI changes from postgres-pglite branch
REL_17_5_WASM-pglite (commit 2194acf356e9b7bf7cff29c4ed4bd6b82b93895d) replayed
onto it; that replay is engine/patches/postgresql-17.11-wasi.patch in the
di-framework source. PostgreSQL, postgres-pglite and the replay patch are
distributed under the PostgreSQL License, reproduced in POSTGRESQL-COPYRIGHT.
The engine is built with the wasipg recipe and its sjlj patches (Apache-2.0;
notice below). The upstream bindings license and WASI adapter license are
reproduced in PGLITE-BINDINGS-LICENSE and WASMTIME-LICENSE. The engine
statically links the pgcrypto extension and OpenSSL libcrypto; their notices
are in PGCRYPTO-NOTICES and the OpenSSL license (Apache-2.0) in
OPENSSL-LICENSE.

Sources:
https://github.com/postgres/postgres/tree/REL_17_11
https://github.com/electric-sql/postgres-pglite/tree/REL_17_5_WASM-pglite
https://github.com/electric-sql/pglite-bindings
https://github.com/moznion/wasipg
https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/tree/v29.0.1
https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/tag/openssl-3.5.9

The engine is compiled with PostgreSQL setjmp/longjmp recovery lowered to
standardized WebAssembly exceptions. di-framework adds a private canonical
ABI bridge, uses WASI randomness instead of a /dev/urandom preopen, and keeps
bootstrap files within the database's persistent filesystem mount. A growable,
bounded memory buffer replaces socket-file spillover for query replies. Backend
startup restores application session defaults after bootstrap and enables
durable writes. The emulated dlopen keeps loaded libraries in a bounded table
instead of writing past the end of an unsized array. Two small changes to the
WASI glue let it compile against 17.11: initdb's frontend SplitGUCList
declaration is renamed where initdb is compiled into the backend, and the
frontend allocator stubs gain the overflow-checked pg_malloc_mul and
pg_realloc_mul. pgcrypto is unmodified: PostgreSQL 17.11 itself refuses
ciphers OpenSSL cannot run (CVE-2026-14663), which in this build includes
Blowfish and CAST5.

The wasipg notice below describes wasipg's own release artifacts, which were
built from REL_17_5_WASM-pglite; this provider uses wasipg's build recipe and
patches with the 17.11 source tree above.

The engine's core module, support files, adapter, and the provider are
composed into one deployable artifact. Engine code executes in the Wasm
runtime; no native database process or socket transport is used.

